Below is a short “road‑map” that shows  

• which tables / columns matter for the requested play‑by‑play summary,  
• the typical filter conditions that will be needed, and  
• ten progressively‑richer BigQuery examples (all limited) that you can run to inspect the data and finally build the chronological scoring log you asked for.  

─────────
Key Tables / Columns  
─────────
`bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`  – every play of every game  
• `season` : restrict to 2014  
• `home_market`, `home_name` : identify the home “Wildcats” team  
• `away_market`, `away_name` : identify the away “Fighting Irish” team  
• `game_id` : once the correct game is found, filter every later query with it  
• `period`, `game_clock`, `elapsed_time_sec` : sort plays chronologically  
• `points_scored` : # points on the play (NULL or 0 if no score)  
• `team_market`, `team_name`, `team_id` : which side scored  
• `event_description` : human‑readable description of the play  
• `shot_made` / `three_point_shot` / `event_type` / `type` : let you isolate *scoring* events (made FGs, FTs, etc.)

─────────
SQL “building blocks”
─────────
```sql
-- 1.  All distinct Sportradar “Wildcats” teams
SELECT DISTINCT home_market, home_name, home_alias
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE  LOWER(home_name)   = 'wildcats'
   OR  LOWER(home_market) LIKE '%wildcats%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  All distinct “Fighting Irish” teams
SELECT DISTINCT away_market, away_name, away_alias
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE  LOWER(away_name)   = 'fighting irish'
   OR  LOWER(away_market) LIKE '%fighting%irish%'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Candidate 2014 games where Wildcats were home & Fighting Irish away
SELECT DISTINCT game_id, scheduled_date, home_market, home_name,
                away_market, away_name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE  season = 2014
  AND  (LOWER(home_name)  = 'wildcats' OR LOWER(home_market) LIKE '%wildcats%')
  AND  (LOWER(away_name)  = 'fighting irish' OR LOWER(away_market) LIKE '%fighting%irish%')
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Peek at every play for the chosen game (replace <GAME_ID>)
SELECT period, game_clock, elapsed_time_sec, team_market, team_name,
       points_scored, event_description
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>'
ORDER  BY elapsed_time_sec ASC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Only plays that actually scored points
SELECT period, game_clock, elapsed_time_sec, team_market, points_scored,
       event_description
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>'
  AND  points_scored > 0
ORDER  BY elapsed_time_sec ASC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Add running points *per team* (window function)
SELECT period, game_clock, elapsed_time_sec,
       team_market, points_scored,
       SUM(points_scored) OVER(PARTITION BY team_id
                               ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec)  AS running_team_pts,
       event_description
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>'
  AND  points_scored > 0
ORDER  BY elapsed_time_sec ASC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Pivot the two running scores so they sit on the same row
WITH scoring AS (
  SELECT elapsed_time_sec, game_clock, period,
         team_market,
         points_scored,
         SUM(points_scored) OVER(PARTITION BY team_id
                                 ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec) AS running_pts,
         event_description
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
  WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>' AND points_scored > 0
)
SELECT game_clock,
       MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Wildcats%'     THEN running_pts END)
         AS wildcats_score,
       MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Fighting Irish%' THEN running_pts END)
         AS fighting_irish_score,
       ANY_VALUE(team_market)  AS scoring_team,
       ANY_VALUE(event_description) AS event_description
FROM   scoring
GROUP  BY elapsed_time_sec, game_clock
ORDER  BY elapsed_time_sec
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Verify final score to be sure cumulative logic is correct
SELECT MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Wildcats%'      THEN running_pts END) AS final_wildcats,
       MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Fighting Irish%' THEN running_pts END) AS final_irish
FROM (
  SELECT team_market,
         SUM(points_scored) OVER(PARTITION BY team_id ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec) AS running_pts
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
  WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>' AND points_scored > 0
);
```

```sql
-- 9.  Nice chronological list with period label (no row limit now)
SELECT CONCAT('P', period, ' – ', game_clock)        AS game_clock_display,
       wildcats_score, fighting_irish_score,
       scoring_team, event_description
FROM (
  -- use same CTE as in #7 but without LIMIT
  WITH scoring AS (
    SELECT elapsed_time_sec, period, game_clock,
           team_market, points_scored,
           SUM(points_scored) OVER(PARTITION BY team_id
                                   ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec) AS running_pts,
           event_description
    FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
    WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>' AND points_scored > 0
  )
  SELECT elapsed_time_sec,
         game_clock,
         period,
         MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Wildcats%'      THEN running_pts END) AS wildcats_score,
         MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Fighting Irish%' THEN running_pts END) AS fighting_irish_score,
         ANY_VALUE(team_market)  AS scoring_team,
         ANY_VALUE(event_description) AS event_description
  FROM   scoring
  GROUP  BY elapsed_time_sec, period, game_clock
)
ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec;
```

```sql
-- 10.  (Final form) Everything requested, perfectly ordered
SELECT game_clock, wildcats_score, fighting_irish_score,
       scoring_team, event_description
FROM (
  WITH scoring AS (
    SELECT elapsed_time_sec, game_clock,
           team_market, points_scored,
           SUM(points_scored) OVER(PARTITION BY team_id
                                   ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec) AS running_pts,
           event_description
    FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
    WHERE  game_id = '<GAME_ID>'            --  <-- fill in from query #3
      AND  points_scored > 0
  )
  SELECT elapsed_time_sec, game_clock,
         MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Wildcats%'      THEN running_pts END) AS wildcats_score,
         MAX(CASE WHEN team_market LIKE '%Fighting Irish%' THEN running_pts END) AS fighting_irish_score,
         ANY_VALUE(team_market)  AS scoring_team,
         ANY_VALUE(event_description) AS event_description
  FROM   scoring
  GROUP  BY elapsed_time_sec, game_clock
)
ORDER BY elapsed_time_sec;
```

Run the first three queries to identify the exact `game_id` for the 2014 contest with home “Wildcats” and away “Fighting Irish”, substitute that ID into the later statements, and query #10 will yield the complete, chronologically‑ordered scoring summary with running totals for both sides.
